            <ArticleTitle>Grey Turner's and Cullen's signs induced by spontaneous hemorrhage of the abdominal wall after coughing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>115-117</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4174/astr.2017.93.2.115</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Grey Turner's and Cullen's signs are rare clinical signs, which most appear in patients with severe acute pancreatitis. The present patient complained of abdominal pain after coughing. However, contrast-enhanced CT revealed a hemorrhage of the abdominal wall. Therefore, spontaneous hemorrhage of the abdominal wall was diagnosed. The patient recovered through immobilization and hemostasis therapy. This case report and literature review aims to remind clinicians of manifestations and treatment of spontaneous hemorrhage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
